@startuml arch_hooks
!include palette.iuml
hide footbox
title What do the hooks do around the agent's work?

participant "Agent tool" as tool
participant "guard_bash.py" as guard
participant "repeated_failure.py" as failure
participant "after_edit.py" as edit
participant "compact_brief.py" as brief
participant "session_refresh.py" as refresh
participant "progress_check.py" as progress
participant "git" as git
collections ".private/" as notes
participant "claim_check.py" as claim
participant "transcript" as transcript

== Claude Code: before a compaction ==
tool -> brief : payload (cwd, trigger)
brief -> notes : newest progress\nand handoff files
brief -> git : branch, status
brief --> tool : exit 0 always: what\nthe summary must keep

== Claude Code and Codex: after a compaction or resume ==
tool -> refresh : payload (cwd, source)
refresh -> notes : newest progress\nand handoff files\n(a worktree: the main\ncheckout's)
refresh -> git : branch, status,\nlast 5 commits,\nother worktrees
refresh --> tool : stale-memory reminder,\nafter a compaction "invoke\nthe workflow skill again",\ngit state, notes and\n"re-read the progress log"

== Before a shell command ==
tool -> guard : payload with the command
guard -> guard : split into\nsimple commands
alt a gate bypass, any push or publish,\na gh command that is not read or\nlocal, or one that prints the token\n(every tool)
  guard --> tool : exit 2, reason on stderr;\nCopilot CLI: also a deny\ndecision as JSON on stdout;\nAntigravity CLI: exit 0\nand a deny decision
else nothing to block
  guard --> tool : exit 0 (Antigravity CLI:\nan allow decision)
end
note over tool, guard : Claude Code: a guard that\ncannot run blocks the command

== Claude Code: after a shell command fails ==
tool -> failure : payload (session, command, error)
failure -> failure : count it per session\nby command and whole\nerror, each word with\na digit masked
opt the third identical failure or later
  failure --> tool : context: stop, restate the\nevidence, change approach
end

== After an edit ==
tool -> edit : payload with the file\nand the new text
edit -> edit : dashes in the new text;\nsyntax of a .py, .json\nor .toml file; clang-format\non a C or C++ file
alt a dash, a syntax error or\na clang-format failure
  edit --> tool : exit 2, report on stderr;\nCopilot CLI: exit 0, report\nas additionalContext;\nAntigravity CLI: exit 0, {},\nreport on stderr only
else nothing wrong
  edit --> tool : exit 0, notice if reformatted
end

== When the agent ends its turn: Claude Code and Codex (progress check), Claude Code (claim check) ==
tool -> progress : payload (cwd, stop_hook_active)
progress -> git : branch <type>/<slug>,\nits own commits
progress -> notes : progress/<slug>.*
opt not yet continued, and a commit\nnewer than the log or not in it
  progress --> tool : block once: record each\nstep, its commit and check
end
tool -> claim : payload (last message,\ntranscript path)
claim -> transcript : last 4 MB
claim -> claim : sort calls after\nthe last edit\n(guard's parser)
opt not yet continued, a "tests pass"\nclaim, and no passing run\nafter the last edit
  claim --> tool : block once: run the\ntests or say they were not
end

legend right
  Solid arrow: a call
  Dashed arrow: the reply
endlegend
@enduml
